#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Real fish for the simulator: scanned models, reduced, oriented, credited.

    hardware/.venv/bin/python tools/fish-models/build <dir of .glb> [--box]

Grown fish (fishform.py) are shapes; these are fish. Each entry in MODELS
names a species sheet (fish_species.py), the Sketchfab model that stands for
it, and how close that model is to the species — the same species, its genus,
or its family — because a stand-in has to say it is one.

The scans come from Sketchfab through Objaverse (allenai/objaverse on Hugging
Face): most are ffish.asia's CC0 photogrammetry of real specimens, a few are
CC-BY and carry their author. Each is reduced to a few thousand faces in
Blender on the box (tools/fish-models/reduce.py: collapse decimation keeps the
UVs right across seams), then here:

  **oriented**: the longest axis is nose to tail, the shortest side to side;
  the head is the end with the bigger cross-section (a tail is a fin), and
  the back is the darker side (countershading) unless MODELS says otherwise;
  **sized**: a metre nose to tail, centred, as every fish body is, so that the
  runtime scales it to each fish's own length;
  **packed** into services/sim-runtime/coral/fauna/<species>/: model.npz
  (points, faces, uv), texture.jpg, and source.json with the credit.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import io
import json
import pathlib
import subprocess
import sys

import numpy as np

